{
  "dom_id": "step-q53011",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224458/assets/6ada3cc0fcd02f363da922e9537d3f832cd616886da84f63e65085bd271aa3e0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the rectangle above?\n\nI. $∠BCD$ is not a right angle.\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are parallel.\n\nIII. $BC=CD.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. A rectangle is a parallelogram where all angles are right. Therefore, $∠BCD$ is a right angle.\n\n- Statement II is true. The opposite sides of a rectangle are parallel, so $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are parallel.\n\n- Statement III is false. Opposite sides of a rectangle are congruent, however, $BC$ and $CD$ are adjacent and we see that $BC\\ne CD.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true.",
